  "description": "Empirical Macdonald-norm probe for Casimir prefactor via Cherednik DAHA-derived candidates.  Computes Macdonald norm ⟨P_λ, P_λ⟩_{q,t} via the arm-leg formula for all partitions λ of size 1..5 at substrate q ≈ 1.110 and seven t-specializations (t=q, q², q^½, 1, q⁻¹, q^{1/3}, q^{2/3}).  Then forms three natural Cherednik-zeta candidate combinations: Σ⟨P_λ⟩^{-1}, Σ⟨P_λ⟩, and alternating-sign Σ.  Tests direct match vs π²/720 AND geometric-multiplier-applied match vs π²/720.  Reports count of sub-1% matches.  Null result reinforces sub-problem 3's genuine open status — even the Macdonald-norm route doesn't easily yield the Casimir prefactor at substrate.",
